ed from commit fee686b74a9c115d3c4c851eb6613d1378ad0e0c) [strassek: sdhci-pci-core.c doesn't exist in our tree] Signed-off-by: Kevin Strasser &lt;kevin.strasser@intel.com&gt;  BUG=b:35774937 TEST=Check that max eMMC read latency on Cave/Caroline is under 30ms TEST=`fio --name=trest --size=4k --readwrite=read`  Change-Id: I75ecb09a550d02310e63dc0c54f71906339ca43c Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/486955 Commit-Ready: Kevin Strasser &lt;kevin.strasser@intel.com&gt; Tested-by: Russ Sage &lt;russ.sage@intel.com&gt; Reviewed-by: Sonny Rao &lt;sonnyrao@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="486955" owner_email="kevin.strasser@intel.com" pass_count="0" patch_number="1" project="chromiumos/third_party/kernel" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/kernel" ref="refs/changes/55/486955/1" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="chromeos-3.18" change_id="Iedb13db830b10055fac57444c6fa912269fe95e3" commit="d7b731554d8d9fd7de8757c37a76bde0f0fe2fe8" commit_message="FROMLIST: mmc: sdhci: Optimize delay loops  The delay loops for reset and clock enable always take at least 1 ms because they use mdelay(1). However they can take a lot less time e.g. less than 50us. Use ktime and reduce the delay to 10 microseconds per loop.  Signed-off-by: Adrian Hunter &lt;adrian.hunter@intel.com&gt; (am from https://patchwork.kernel.org/patch/9634743/) Signed-off-by: Kevin Strasser &lt;kevin.strasser@intel.com&gt;  BUG=b:35774937 TEST=Check that max eMMC read latency on Cave/Caroline is under 30ms TEST=`fio --name=trest --size=4k --readwrite=read`  Change-Id: Iedb13db830b10055fac57444c6fa912269fe95e3 Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/486956 Commit-Ready: Kevin Strasser &lt;kevin.strasser@intel.com&gt; Tested-by: Russ Sage &lt;russ.sage@intel.com&gt; Reviewed-by: Sonny Rao &lt;sonnyrao@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="486956" owner_email="kevin.strasser@intel.com" pass_count="0" 