t_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/kernel" ref="refs/changes/26/495226/1" remote="cros" total_fail_count="1"/><pending_commit branch="chromeos-3.14" change_id="Ief497d5b36fa0266dd7d77a1168eaeba47dad3fc" commit="3498afe44671024f41b2be7fd8e852f4883fea56" commit_message="UPSTREAM: perf: Tighten (and fix) the grouping condition  The fix from 9fc81d87420d (&quot;perf: Fix events installation during moving group&quot;) was incomplete in that it failed to recognise that creating a group with events for different CPUs is semantically broken -- they cannot be co-scheduled.  Furthermore, it leads to real breakage where, when we create an event for CPU Y and then migrate it to form a group on CPU X, the code gets confused where the counter is programmed -- triggered in practice as well by me via the perf fuzzer.  Fix this by tightening the rules for creating groups. Only allow grouping of counters that can be co-scheduled in the same context. This means for the same task and/or the same cpu.  BUG=b:34515362, b:37858885 TEST=Build and run  Change-Id: Ief497d5b36fa0266dd7d77a1168eaeba47dad3fc Fixes: 9fc81d87420d (&quot;perf: Fix events installation during moving group&quot;) Signed-off-by: Peter Zijlstra (Intel) &lt;peterz@infradead.org&gt; Cc: Arnaldo Carvalho de Melo &lt;acme@kernel.org&gt; Cc: Jiri Olsa &lt;jolsa@redhat.com&gt; Cc: Linus Torvalds &lt;torvalds@linux-foundation.org&gt; Link: http://lkml.kernel.org/r/20150123125834.090683288@infradead.org Signed-off-by: Ingo Molnar &lt;mingo@kernel.org&gt; Signed-off-by: Guenter Roeck &lt;groeck@chromium.org&gt; (cherry picked from commit c3c87e770458) Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/494167 Reviewed-by: Dylan Reid &lt;dgreid@chromium.org&gt; (cherry picked from commit d4c60d8c9944231fdf3bddd8a1076f9b3ce739ab) Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/494247 " fail_count="2" gerrit_number="494247" owner_email="groeck@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="1" project="chromiumos/third_party/kernel" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/kernel" ref="refs/changes/47/494247/1" remote="cros" total_fail_count="2"/><lkgm version="9521.0.0-rc2"/></manifest>